{{also|Buono}}
==Italian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|it|bono||Tuscan}}<ref>{{R:roa:AIS|buono; buona; buoni|710|place=523}}</ref>

===Etymology===
{{inh+|it|la|bonus}}. {{doublet|it|bonus}}, a later borrowing.

===Pronunciation===
{{it-pr|buòno<audio:It-buono.ogg>}}

===Adjective===
{{it-adj|sup=buonissimo|dim=bonìno<q:informal>,buonìno,bonétto<q:archaic>|aug=bonóne<q:informal>}}

# [[good]], [[nice]] (in general)
## [[righteous]], [[moral]]
##: {{uxa|it|Le sue '''buone''' azioni non saranno mai dimenticate.|His '''good''' deeds will never be forgotten.}}
## {{q|of the weather}} [[good]], [[nice]]; [[favorable]] and [[sunny]]
##: {{ant|it|brutto|cattivo}}
##: {{uxa|it|'''Buon''' tempo, oggi.|'''Nice''' weather, today.}}
## [[competent]], [[talented]], [[skillful]]
##: {{syn|it|ottimo|bravo}}
##: {{ant|it|pessimo|orribile}}
##: {{uxa|it|Un '''buon''' violinista|A '''good''' violinist}}
##: {{uxa|it|Sei '''buono''' solo a perdere tempo!|The only thing you're '''good''' at is wasting time!}}
## that [[works]] well for its [[purpose]]
##: {{ant|it|brutto|pessimo}}
##: {{uxa|it|Hai proprio una '''buona''' memoria.|You've unequivocally got a '''good''' memory.}}
## {{q|of animals or children}} [[well behaved]]
##: {{uxa|it|Ragazzi, '''buoni'''!|Boys, '''composure'''!}}
## [[intrinsically]] [[good]] or [[appreciated]]
## [[suitable]], [[valid]] {{rfex|it}} <!--- at this point I'm afraid this sense is just too specific and could easily otherwise just be assimilated into or appropriated as another already present sense? See yourselves --->
# [[tasting]] good
#: {{syn|it|gustoso}}
#: {{uxa|it|Questa pizza è davvero '''buona'''.|This pizza is very undoubtedly '''good'''.}}
# [[nice]], [[kind]], [[benevolent]]
## [[ingenuous]], [[overly]] [[nice]]
##: {{syn|it|debole}}
##: {{uxa|it|Nella vita bisogna essere '''buoni''', sì, ma fino a un certo punto.|In life one must be '''nice''', sure, but [only] up to a certain point.}}
## [[lenient]], [[lax]]
##: {{syn|it|clemente}} 
##: {{nearsyn|it|indulgente}}
##: {{uxa|it|Anzi, mi dovreste ringraziare perché non avrei dovuto essere così '''buono'''!|The exact opposite, you guys should be thanking me because I shouldn't have been this '''lenient'''!}}

====Usage notes====
* The [[apocopic]] form {{m|it|buon}} and (optionally) the contracted form {{m|it|buon'}} are used before masculine and feminine singular nouns, respectively, in the same manner as the indefinite article (i.e. {{m|it|buon giorno}}, {{m|it|[[buon]] [[amico]]}} but {{m|it|[[buono]] [[zio]]}}, {{m|it|[[buona]] [[sera]]}} but {{m|it|[[buon']][[amica]]}}, etc.).

